      "content": "\"Taking the weight off yourself\" means stopping the relentless, exhausting effort to be perfect when you are clearly not. You are a flawed human, and that flaw is not a failure that needs fixing; it's just part of the mess of being alive. Instead of trying to fix everything, maybe you can just stop trying to be the hero they need, because that role is impossible. Sometimes, the kindest thing you can do for them is to let them be in a world where you are simply *present*, not constantly fighting to be adequate.",
